ass=\"md-ellipsis\">","</span>","</a>"]},{"s":34223,"e":34374,"k":"block","t":"\n  KTPH000\n    KTPH001\n      \n        Your consent record\n      \n    KTPH002\n  KTPH003\n  \n","f":["<a href=\"#your-consent-record\" class=\"md-nav__link\">","<span class=\"md-ellipsis\">","</span>","</a>"]},{"s":34744,"e":34894,"k":"block","t":"Anonymous data for application optimizationKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#anonymous-data-for-application-optimization\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":34903,"e":35166,"k":"block","t":"korTTY can collect KTPH000anonymous usage statisticsKTPH001 to help decide which features are worth improving and to find crashes and frequent errors. This is entirely optional, switched KTPH002off by defaultKTPH003, and can be turned on or off at any time.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":35174,"e":35281,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"Anonymous telemetry consent and data flow\" src=\"../assets/diagrams/telemetry-consent-flow.svg\" />"]},{"s":35304,"e":35384,"k":"block","t":"OverviewKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#overview\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":35399,"e":35605,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Opt-in.KTPH001 Nothing is collected unless you explicitly agree. You are asked once, together with the master-password setup on first launch; existing installations are asked once after unlocking.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":35615,"e":35716,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Anonymous.KTPH001 No account, no login, and no persistent device identifier is transmitted.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":35726,"e":35931,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Revocable.KTPH001 You can change your decision at any time under KTPH002Settings → PrivacyKTPH003. Turning it off stops collection immediately and discards any data that has not yet been sent.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":35970,"e":36068,"k":"block","t":"What is collectedKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#what-is-collected\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":36099,"e":36103,"k":"block","t":"Data","f":[]},{"s":36113,"e":36120,"k":"block","t":"Example","f":[]},{"s":36158,"e":36169,"k":"block","t":"Event names","f":[]},{"s":36179,"e":36241,"k":"block","t":"app start, feature used (e.g. a tool opened, a backup created)","f":[]},{"s":36262,"e":36288,"k":"block","t":"Aggregate counts and flags","f":[]},{"s":36298,"e":36349,"k":"block","t":"number of open terminal tabs, whether AI is enabled","f":[]},{"s":36370,"e":36381,"k":"block","t":"App version","f":[]},{"s":36417,"e":36445,"k":"block","t":"Operating system and version","f":[]},{"s":36455,"e":36482,"k":"block","t":"macOS 15, Windows 11, Linux","f":[]},{"s":36503,"e":36515,"k":"block","t":"App language","f":[]},{"s":36525,"e":36531,"k":"block","t":"de, en","f":[]},{"s":36552,"e":36575,"k":"block","t":"An anonymous session ID","f":[]},{"s":36585,"e":36661,"k":"block","t":"a random number regenerated on every launch and after one hour of inactivity","f":[]},{"s":36694,"e":36839,"k":"block","t":"The session ID is KTPH000notKTPH001 a persistent identifier: it is newly generated each time and cannot be traced back to you across launches.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":36877,"e":36987,"k":"block","t":"What is never collectedKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#what-is-never-collected\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":36996,"e":37040,"k":"block","t":"korTTY never transmits any of the following:","f":[]},{"s":37054,"e":37123,"k":"block","t":"Hostnames, IP addresses, usernames, or connection names and addresses","f":[]},{"s":37133,"e":37173,"k":"block","t":"File names, paths, or directory contents","f":[]},{"s":37183,"e":37243,"k":"block","t":"Snippet content, terminal output, or AI prompt and chat text","f":[]},{"s":37253,"e":37295,"k":"block","t":"Passwords, SSH keys, GPG keys, or API keys","f":[]},{"s":37305,"e":37383,"k":"block","t":"Error messages (only the type of error and the korTTY class where it occurred)","f":[]},{"s":37424,"e":37526,"k":"block","t":"Where the data goesKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#where-the-data-goes\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":37535,"e":37967,"k":"block","t":"Usage statistics are processed by KTPH001KTPH002AptabaseKTPH003KTPH004, an open-source, privacy-first analytics service. korTTY uses Aptabase's KTPH005EU regionKTPH006 (KTPH000), so the data is processed on servers located in the European Union in compliance with the KTPH007GDPRKTPH008. See the KTPH009Aptabase privacy policyKTPH010 for details.","f":["<code>eu.aptabase.com</code>","<strong>","<a href=\"https://aptabase.com\">","</a>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<a href=\"https://aptabase.com/legal/privacy\">","</a>"]},{"s":37975,"e":38306,"k":"block","t":"If no connection is available, events are cached locally in KTPH000 and sent later — including after a restart — so a temporary lack of connectivity does not lose or block anything. This offline cache holds only the same anonymous events; it is discarded if you opt out, and events older than three days are dropped.","f":["<code>~/.kortty</code>"]},{"s":38343,"e":38451,"k":"block","t":"Why korTTY collects itKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#why-kortty-collects-it\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":38460,"e":38545,"k":"block","t":"The goal is to make korTTY better with real, anonymous evidence instead of guesswork:","f":[]},{"s":38559,"e":38655,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Prioritize featuresKTPH001 that people actually use, and retire ones that nobody does.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":38665,"e":38756,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Find crashes and frequent errorsKTPH001 so they can be fixed in the next release.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":38766,"e":38836,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Measure whether releases improve stabilityKTPH001 over time.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":38870,"e":38958,"k":"block","t":"Your choicesKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#your-choices\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":38973,"e":39094,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000First launch:KTPH001 the setup dialog for the master password includes an opt-in checkbox and this information.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":39104,"e":39246,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Any time:KTPH001 open KTPH002Settings → PrivacyKTPH003 to enable or disable collection. The same page links back to this chapter.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":39256,"e":39366,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Turning it offKTPH001 stops all collection immediately and discards data that has not yet been sent.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":39381,"e":39466,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"Privacy settings tab\" src=\"../assets/screenshots/settings/telemetry.png\" />"]},{"s":39500,"e":39602,"k":"block","t":"Your consent recordKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#your-consent-record\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":39611,"e":39937,"k":"block","t":"Your decision and the date it was made are stored locally in KTPH000 (see KTPH001Configuration filesKTPH002) as a record of consent. If a future korTTY version changes what is collected, you will be asked again so your choice always reflects the current scope.","f":["<code>~/.kortty/global-settings.xml</code>","<a href=\"../reference/config-files.html\">","</a>"]},{"s":40815,"e":40830,"k":"text","t":"\n  Back to top\n","f":[]},{"s":41073,"e":41114,"k":"text","t":"MIT-licensed · Developed by Daniel Mengel","f":[]},{"s":41160,"e":41172,"k":"text","t":"\n    korTTY ","f":[]},{"s":41180,"e":41186,"k":"text","t":"v2.7.0","f":[]}]}